  "packageHashAlgorithm": "SHA512",
  "packageSize": 661828,
  "published": "2026-10-29T10:24:45.86Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "v5.7.0: a Blazor Server circuit follows the renewals of its own session's cookie, and what blocked users is fixed. Behaviour change: once the expiry it took passes, a circuit adopts the latest expiry a cookie of its own session (same session id, same principal) presented and the library accepted, never a computed one; keep an HTTP request going while the user is active (the demo ships a keep-alive recipe). Behaviour change (security): the cookie's security stamp is checked on the library's own cadence, so a revocation reaches a cookie in use even when sliding expiration keeps renewing it. Requests to a hub no longer renew the sliding cookie. Over long polling a circuit sees the signed-in user with the cut of its cookie. Inside a circuit the page gate reads the scope from the RouteData passed as the authorization resource (pass Resource=\"@routeData\" under AnyScope). New MyIdentityModuleDefinition.TenantWideOnly and MyIdentityPermissionOptions.IsTenantWideOnly; the identity module is declared tenant-wide-only by default. New opt-in MyIdentity:Authentication:Cookies:AbsoluteSessionLifetimeMinutes. New IMyIdentityUserService.RestoreAsync undoes a soft delete into the tenant the account left, disabled; it needs the new MyIdentityUser.DeletedFromTenantId column: add and apply a migration (the first mandatory one of 5.x). An impersonation continues the admin's session and stopping it keeps the admin's persistence. A reset with a valid token clears MustChangePassword. A decision point that re-enters the delegated read throws instead of recursing. ChangeOwnPasswordAsync throws inside a unit of work. Breaking: a hand-written IMyIdentityUserService adds RestoreAsync. The package validation baseline is 5.6.0. Upgrading from 5.6.0: MyIdentity/UPGRADE.md §51.",
